<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.CompilerArchitecture
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>CompilerArchitecture</name>
  <type>doc:CompilerArchitecture</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to the compiler pipeline</is>

  <documentation>
    Overview only — normative Urmodell / Pragmatic / BomBuilder rules live in docs/01_bom_core.md;
    pipeline stages and packages in docs/06_compiler.md; system layout in docs/00_system.md.

    Sketch: BML → Parser → Urmodell (immutable Canonical BOM) → Validator pragmatic fork /
    Framework Utilities / Render Target pipeline → target output. Serializer reads the Urmodell only.
    Validation Stages 1–3 (Parser / Validator / Renderer) — glossary in 06_compiler.md.
    Self-hosting: CLI bootstraps TypeRegistry from framework BML before user projects.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="06_compiler.md" relation="DeepDive">
      Compiler pipeline — stages, packages, error handling, testing strategy.
    </see>
    <see file="01_bom_core.md" relation="DeepDive">
      Fundamental architecture principles — immutable BOM, utilities, validation pipeline.
    </see>
    <see file="00_system.md" relation="DeepDive">
      Three-layer system architecture and package overview.
    </see>
    <see file="13_bml_to_bom_mapping.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      BML → BOM mapping algorithm — parser implementation contract.
    </see>
    <see file="12_bom_object_model.md" relation="DeepDive">
      Formal BOM data structures — BomDocument, BlockDefinition.
    </see>
    <see file="14_compiler_runtime.md" relation="DeepDive">
      Compiler runtime — bootstrap, RenderContext, compile I/O model.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:RendererFreedom" relation="ReadNext">
      Next reading step — renderer decides manifestation, not BlockML.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
